  "verdict": "SCIENTIFIC_NEGATIVE",
  "recommendation": "keep-flagged",
  "rationale": [
    "No aggregate speed win: geo-mean two-pass/default p50 wall-clock ratio 0.997 over 15 clips (4 clips >5% faster, best 0.63; 7 clips >5% slower, worst 1.31). The adaptive schedule saves frames on some clips and adds frames on others (consistent with C08's afn-sasebo-rally1 finding).",
    "Output equivalence FAILS: 14/15 clips have report field diffs beyond tolerance (up to 75 fields), including contact status, strokePrediction, and temporal phase boundaries; 5/15 clips have byte-level mismatches on shared paddle-detection frames (e.g. yt-94KNxpNTyCw 16/60 shared frames differ). Determinism control confirms the default path is deterministic, so divergence is attributable to the two-pass path.",
    "Promotion (default flip) is therefore ruled out without an accuracy study showing two-pass outputs are as good or better - which requires labeled contact/stroke ground truth that this label-blind corpus cannot provide (and Mac/Apple Vision canonical runs remain BLOCKED_EXTERNAL).",
    "Removal is not recommended yet: the path is correct-by-construction on its own schedule, shows 18-37% wall-clock wins on 4/15 clips, and remains the only adaptive-sampling implementation; it stays behind --two-pass (default OFF) until an accuracy-based comparison exists."
  ],
  "honestyNotes": [
    "All numbers are LINUX-CPU; no Mac/iPhone/Apple Vision claims.",
    "Pose seeds are MediaPipe-derived constant inputs for latency comparison only; per-clip 'not_analyzable'/'abstained' outcomes are the pipeline's honest gates and were identical between arms on every clip.",
    "Fresh-candidate pool used label-blind; no labeling, no tuning, held-out clips untouched."
  ]
}
